-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part ssc1 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for the seat layer ssc1-seat.l4: the facts a person in the seat would state, and the answer the text gives.
-- Every expected value is written from the text beside the assertion. The earnings limits below are STAND-IN figures chosen to make the
-- boundaries easy to see (lower earnings limit 100, primary threshold 200, upper earnings limit 1000, secondary threshold 150); the
-- real figures are set by regulations for each tax year and are asked of the person.
-- Argument order of a question is the order of its GIVEN list in ssc1-seat.l4.

§ `Cases for the seat`

§§ `Who is an earner (ss 1 to 3)`

-- Asha works in a shop in Great Britain under a contract of service: an employed earner, and not a self-employed earner.
#ASSERT `Under section 2(1)(a), am I an employed earner` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2(1)(b), am I a self-employed earner` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Bilal is a freelance designer in Great Britain with no contract of service and no office: self-employed.
#ASSERT `Under section 2(1)(a), am I an employed earner` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2(1)(b), am I a self-employed earner` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Chen holds an unpaid elective office: the office has no earnings, so not an employed earner (the definition says "with ... earnings"); gainfully employed otherwise than in employed earner's employment, so self-employed.
#ASSERT `Under section 2(1)(a), am I an employed earner` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2(1)(b), am I a self-employed earner` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Dana holds an office that carries earnings: an employed earner.
#ASSERT `Under section 2(1)(a), am I an employed earner` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Eli works abroad under a contract of service: not gainfully employed in Great Britain, so neither.
#ASSERT `Under section 2(1)(a), am I an employed earner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 2(1)(b), am I a self-employed earner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Fay is not gainfully employed.
#ASSERT `Under section 2(1)(a), am I an employed earner` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 2(5): a week during any part of which Bilal is self-employed is treated as one of self-employment; the text says nothing of a week with none.
#ASSERT `Under section 2(5), am I treated as a self-employed earner for a week` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 2(5), am I treated as a self-employed earner for a week` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 3(1)(a): what Asha is paid for her work is earnings; whether something that is not remuneration or profit from an employment is earnings is not answered ("includes").
#ASSERT `Under section 3(1)(a), is what I receive earnings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 3(1)(a), is what I receive earnings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 1(6)(a): a person who does not fulfil the residence conditions is not liable to pay Class 2; one who does is not thereby made liable ("unless"); Class 4 is not among the classes named.
#ASSERT `Under section 1(6)(a), am I liable to pay a contribution of this class` `Class 2` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 1(6)(a), am I liable to pay a contribution of this class` `Class 2` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 1(6)(a), am I liable to pay a contribution of this class` `Class 4` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 1(6)(b), am I entitled to pay Class 3 contributions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 1(6)(b), am I entitled to pay Class 3 contributions` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Payments treated as earnings (ss 4 to 4C)`

-- s 4(1)(a): Gina is paid statutory sick pay by her employer in satisfaction of her entitlement; if the sum is not paid in satisfaction of an entitlement the section is silent.
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(a), is a statutory payment I receive treated as pay from employed earner's employment` `statutory sick pay` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(a), is a statutory payment I receive treated as pay from employed earner's employment` `statutory maternity pay` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(a), is a statutory payment I receive treated as pay from employed earner's employment` `statutory sick pay` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4A(7): a worker under an obligation personally to perform services is treated as performing them; one who neither performs nor is so obliged is not addressed.
#ASSERT `Under section 4A(7), am I treated as performing the services` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 4A(7), am I treated as performing the services` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 4A(7), am I treated as performing the services` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Class 1 contributions (ss 5 to 9B)`

-- Hana is over 16, employed in Great Britain under a contract of service, resident in Great Britain, with no Class 1B and not past pensionable age.
-- Arguments: pay, tax year, tax week, LEL, PT, UEL, ST, over 16, gainfully employed, in GB, contract of service, office, office carries earnings, residence conditions, Class 1B payable, paid after pensionable age, regulations prescribe otherwise.
-- s 6(1)(a): payable if the amount paid exceeds the primary threshold (200): 201 yes; exactly 200 does not exceed it.
#ASSERT `Under section 6(1)(a), must I pay a primary Class 1 contribution on these earnings` 201 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 6(1)(a), must I pay a primary Class 1 contribution on these earnings` 200 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 6(2): no primary contribution where a Class 1B contribution is payable on the earnings.
#ASSERT `Under section 6(1)(a), must I pay a primary Class 1 contribution on these earnings` 201 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 1(6)(a): no liability without the residence conditions.
#ASSERT `Under section 6(1)(a), must I pay a primary Class 1 contribution on these earnings` 201 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 6(3): no primary contribution on earnings paid after pensionable age, except as prescribed; where regulations prescribe otherwise the bar falls away and s 6(1)(a) stands.
#ASSERT `Under section 6(1)(a), must I pay a primary Class 1 contribution on these earnings` 201 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 6(1)(a), must I pay a primary Class 1 contribution on these earnings` 201 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 6(1): an earner not over 16 is outside the opening words, so the text is silent.
#ASSERT `Under section 6(1)(a), must I pay a primary Class 1 contribution on these earnings` 201 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 8(1): the main primary percentage (8%) of the earnings above the primary threshold up to the upper earnings limit, 2% above that.
#ASSERT `Under section 8(1), how much primary Class 1 contribution must I pay on these earnings` 201 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.08
#ASSERT `Under section 8(1), how much primary Class 1 contribution must I pay on these earnings` 1000 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 64
#ASSERT `Under section 8(1), how much primary Class 1 contribution must I pay on these earnings` 1500 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 74
-- s 8(1) speaks only "where a primary Class 1 contribution is payable": at the threshold, or with a Class 1B contribution, no amount is given.
#ASSERT `Under section 8(1), how much primary Class 1 contribution must I pay on these earnings` 200 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 8(1), how much primary Class 1 contribution must I pay on these earnings` 1500 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6(1)(b): the employer owes a secondary contribution if the amount exceeds the secondary threshold (150): 151 yes; exactly 150 no; a Class 1B contribution bars it.
#ASSERT `Under section 6(1)(b), must my employer pay a secondary Class 1 contribution on these earnings` 151 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 6(1)(b), must my employer pay a secondary Class 1 contribution on these earnings` 150 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 6(1)(b), must my employer pay a secondary Class 1 contribution on these earnings` 151 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 9(1): the secondary percentage (15%) of the earnings above the secondary threshold: (250 - 150) x 15% = 15.
-- Arguments after the fifteen common ones (pay to the Class 1B answer): in an age group, age-related percentage, under 25, apprentice, upper threshold for the age group exists, its amount, upper threshold for apprentices exists, its amount.
#ASSERT `Under section 9(1), how much secondary Class 1 contribution must my employer pay on these earnings` 250 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 15
-- s 9A: an earner in a specified age group carries the age-related percentage (stand-in 5%): 100 x 5% = 5.
#ASSERT `Under section 9(1), how much secondary Class 1 contribution must my employer pay on these earnings` 250 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 15
-- s 9B: a relevant apprentice carries 0%, and above the upper secondary threshold for apprentices (stand-in 1000) the 15% rate: 0 x 850 + 15% x 100 = 15; below it, 0.
#ASSERT `Under section 9(1), how much secondary Class 1 contribution must my employer pay on these earnings` 1100 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 TRUE 1000 EQUALS JUST 15
#ASSERT `Under section 9(1), how much secondary Class 1 contribution must my employer pay on these earnings` 900 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 TRUE 1000 EQUALS JUST 0
-- s 9(1) speaks only "where a secondary Class 1 contribution is payable": at the threshold no amount is given.
#ASSERT `Under section 9(1), how much secondary Class 1 contribution must my employer pay on these earnings` 150 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 9B(2): an earner under 25 employed as an apprentice is a relevant apprentice; one who is not employed as an apprentice, or who is 25 or over, is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 9B(2), am I a relevant apprentice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 9B(2), am I a relevant apprentice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 9B(2), am I a relevant apprentice` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 6A(2): earnings of 100 to 200 (the lower earnings limit to the primary threshold, both ends included) are treated as a primary contribution paid, for contributory benefits.
-- Arguments after the thirteen common ones: purpose, the provision is one in section 21(5A)(a) to (c), a prescribed exception applies.
#ASSERT `Under section 6A(2), am I treated as having paid a primary Class 1 contribution for this week` 100 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 6A(3)(c) any other purposes relating to contributory benefits` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 6A(2), am I treated as having paid a primary Class 1 contribution for this week` 200 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 6A(3)(c) any other purposes relating to contributory benefits` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 6A(2), am I treated as having paid a primary Class 1 contribution for this week` 99.99 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 6A(3)(c) any other purposes relating to contributory benefits` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 6A(2), am I treated as having paid a primary Class 1 contribution for this week` 200.01 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 6A(3)(c) any other purposes relating to contributory benefits` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 6A(2), am I treated as having paid a primary Class 1 contribution for this week` 150 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 6A(3)(a) the purposes of section 14(1)(a)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 6A(2), am I treated as having paid a primary Class 1 contribution for this week` 150 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 6A(3)(b) the purposes of the provisions mentioned in section 21(5A)(a) to (c)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 6A(2), am I treated as having paid a primary Class 1 contribution for this week` 150 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 6A(3)(b) the purposes of the provisions mentioned in section 21(5A)(a) to (c)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 6A(2), am I treated as having paid a primary Class 1 contribution for this week` 150 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 6A(3) any other purpose` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 6A(2), am I treated as having paid a primary Class 1 contribution for this week` 150 2025 10 100 200 1000 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 6A(3)(c) any other purposes relating to contributory benefits` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Class 1A contributions on benefits in kind (ss 10 to 10ZB)`

-- s 10(1): Ivan's employer provides a company car; all four conditions hold, so a Class 1A contribution is payable; if any fails the text is silent.
#ASSERT `Under section 10(1), is a Class 1A contribution payable on the benefits I get from my job` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 10(1), is a Class 1A contribution payable on the benefits I get from my job` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 10(1), is a Class 1A contribution payable on the benefits I get from my job` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 10(4), (5): the Class 1A percentage (the secondary percentage, 15%) of benefits worth 2000 is 300.
#ASSERT `Under section 10(4), how much Class 1A contribution is payable on these benefits` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2000 EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `Under section 10(4), how much Class 1A contribution is payable on these benefits` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 10ZA(3): a third party provides the benefit, not arranged by the employer, in 2005: the provider owes the contribution.
-- Arguments: Class 1A payable, benefit for me or family, provider not my employer, employer did not arrange, sporting testimonial, tax year, notice given, day of notice.
#ASSERT `Under section 10ZA(3), does the person who provides the benefit rather than my employer owe the Class 1A contribution` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2005 FALSE (Date 1 1 2005) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- For the tax year beginning 6 April 2000 only if the provider gave written notice on or before 6 July 2001.
#ASSERT `Under section 10ZA(3), does the person who provides the benefit rather than my employer owe the Class 1A contribution` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2000 TRUE (Date 6 7 2001) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 10ZA(3), does the person who provides the benefit rather than my employer owe the Class 1A contribution` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2000 TRUE (Date 7 7 2001) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 10ZA(3), does the person who provides the benefit rather than my employer owe the Class 1A contribution` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 2000 FALSE (Date 1 1 2001) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A sporting testimonial payment is outside section 10ZA; where the employer arranged the benefit the section does not apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 10ZA(3), does the person who provides the benefit rather than my employer owe the Class 1A contribution` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2005 FALSE (Date 1 1 2005) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 10ZA(3), does the person who provides the benefit rather than my employer owe the Class 1A contribution` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2005 FALSE (Date 1 1 2005) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Class 2 contributions of the self-employed (ss 11 to 12)`

-- Jo is self-employed all year. Arguments of s 11(5B): self-employed in the tax year, in the employment in the week, relevant profits, week before 16, week after pensionable age.
-- s 11(5B): relevant profits of, or exceeding, 7,105 -- exactly 7,105 counts; 7,104.99 does not.
#ASSERT `Under section 11(5B), am I treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution for this week` TRUE TRUE 7105 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 11(5B), am I treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution for this week` TRUE TRUE 7104.99 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 11(7): not for a week before the one in which Jo attains 16, nor after the one in which Jo attains pensionable age.
#ASSERT `Under section 11(5B), am I treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution for this week` TRUE TRUE 9000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 11(5B), am I treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution for this week` TRUE TRUE 9000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 11(1): the section applies if the earner is in employment as a self-employed earner in the tax year.
#ASSERT `Under section 11(5B), am I treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution for this week` FALSE TRUE 9000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 11(6): below the threshold Jo may pay; at or above it Jo need not; regulations may bar payment; the age bars of s 11(7) apply.
-- Arguments: self-employed in the tax year, in the employment in the week, relevant profits, before 16, after pensionable age, regulations bar payment.
#ASSERT `Under section 11(6), may I pay a Class 2 contribution for this week` TRUE TRUE 7104.99 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 11(6), may I pay a Class 2 contribution for this week` TRUE TRUE 7105 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 11(6), may I pay a Class 2 contribution for this week` TRUE TRUE 5000 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 11(6), may I pay a Class 2 contribution for this week` TRUE TRUE 5000 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 11(6), may I pay a Class 2 contribution for this week` FALSE TRUE 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 12: arguments: a s 11(6) contribution, the tax year of the week, the tax year of payment, ordinary contribution, rate in the contribution year, rate at payment, highest rate in the period, regulations apply.
-- Paid in the tax year after the week's: the amount it would have been in the week's year.
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), how much must I pay for a late paid Class 2 contribution` TRUE 2020 2021 TRUE 3.50 3.65 3.65 FALSE EQUALS JUST 3.50
-- Paid after the end of the tax year following the week's, rates differing: the highest weekly rate in the period.
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), how much must I pay for a late paid Class 2 contribution` TRUE 2020 2022 TRUE 3.50 3.65 3.90 FALSE EQUALS JUST 3.90
-- A higher-rate (not ordinary) contribution is not within subsection (3): the amount in the week's year.
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), how much must I pay for a late paid Class 2 contribution` TRUE 2020 2022 FALSE 3.50 3.65 3.90 FALSE EQUALS JUST 3.50
-- Paid in the same tax year, or not a s 11(6) contribution, or subject to regulations: not answered.
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), how much must I pay for a late paid Class 2 contribution` TRUE 2020 2020 TRUE 3.50 3.65 3.90 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), how much must I pay for a late paid Class 2 contribution` FALSE 2020 2022 TRUE 3.50 3.65 3.90 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 12(2), how much must I pay for a late paid Class 2 contribution` TRUE 2020 2022 TRUE 3.50 3.65 3.90 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Class 3 contributions that anyone may pay (ss 13 to 14)`

-- s 13(1): over 16 and entitled under the regulations: yes; not over 16: no; the regulations' conditions not met: not answered.
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), am I entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), am I entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), am I entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 13(4), (6): arguments: tax year it is for, tax year of payment, amount in the earlier year, amount now, highest other amount in between, regulations under (7) apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 13(4), how much must I pay for a Class 3 contribution for an earlier tax year` 2020 2021 18.40 19 19 FALSE EQUALS JUST 18.40
#ASSERT `Under section 13(4), how much must I pay for a Class 3 contribution for an earlier tax year` 2020 2022 18.40 19 19 FALSE EQUALS JUST 18.40
#ASSERT `Under section 13(4), how much must I pay for a Class 3 contribution for an earlier tax year` 2020 2023 18.40 19 19 FALSE EQUALS JUST 19
#ASSERT `Under section 13(4), how much must I pay for a Class 3 contribution for an earlier tax year` 2020 2023 18.40 19 25 FALSE EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `Under section 13(4), how much must I pay for a Class 3 contribution for an earlier tax year` 2020 2023 18.40 18.40 25 FALSE EQUALS JUST 18.40
#ASSERT `Under section 13(4), how much must I pay for a Class 3 contribution for an earlier tax year` 2020 2023 18.40 19 19 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 13(4), how much must I pay for a Class 3 contribution for an earlier tax year` 2020 2020 18.40 19 19 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 13A(1): Kim reached pensionable age on 6 April 2012 (inside the window 6 April 2008 to 5 April 2015), has 22 qualifying years, and asks about the missing year 1990-91.
-- Arguments: day of pensionable age, qualifying years, paid in one year before pensionable age, earnings factor, qualifying earnings factor, missing year, only a time limit bars it, years under this section, day of payment, prescribed conditions satisfied.
-- Eligible, the 1990-91 year is missing, third condition does not apply (pensionable age after 6 April 2010), within 6 tax years, paid before 6 years from pensionable age end on 5 April 2018: entitled.
#ASSERT `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` (Date 6 4 2012) 22 FALSE 0 0 1990 TRUE 3 (Date 1 1 2015) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Paid on 5 April 2018 is not after the end of 6 years; on 6 April 2018 it is.
#ASSERT `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` (Date 6 4 2012) 22 FALSE 0 0 1990 TRUE 3 (Date 5 4 2018) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` (Date 6 4 2012) 22 FALSE 0 0 1990 TRUE 3 (Date 6 4 2018) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No more than 6 tax years: 6 yes, 7 no.
#ASSERT `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` (Date 6 4 2012) 22 FALSE 0 0 1990 TRUE 6 (Date 1 1 2015) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` (Date 6 4 2012) 22 FALSE 0 0 1990 TRUE 7 (Date 1 1 2015) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The second condition needs at least 20 years: 20 yes, 19 not an eligible person, so the grant is not made out.
#ASSERT `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` (Date 6 4 2012) 20 FALSE 0 0 1990 TRUE 3 (Date 1 1 2015) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` (Date 6 4 2012) 19 FALSE 0 0 1990 TRUE 3 (Date 1 1 2015) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The first condition: pensionable age on 5 April 2015 is inside the window, on 6 April 2015 outside it.
#ASSERT `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` (Date 5 4 2015) 22 FALSE 0 0 1990 TRUE 3 (Date 1 1 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` (Date 6 4 2015) 22 FALSE 0 0 1990 TRUE 3 (Date 1 1 2016) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The third condition applies to a person who reached pensionable age before 6 April 2010: an earnings factor at the qualifying level (100) in one paid year satisfies it; 99 does not.
#ASSERT `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` (Date 5 4 2010) 20 TRUE 100 100 1990 TRUE 2 (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` (Date 5 4 2010) 20 TRUE 99 100 1990 TRUE 2 (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A year before 1975-76 is not a missing year; prescribed conditions not met: not answered.
#ASSERT `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` (Date 6 4 2012) 22 FALSE 0 0 1974 TRUE 3 (Date 1 1 2015) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` (Date 6 4 2012) 22 FALSE 0 0 1990 TRUE 3 (Date 1 1 2015) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 14(1): an earnings factor equal to or above the qualifying earnings factor means NOT entitled (JUST FALSE); below it the text does not decide (NOTHING).
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), am I entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution for the tax year` 100 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), am I entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution for the tax year` 101 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), am I entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution for the tax year` 99.99 100 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Class 3A contributions for units of additional pension (ss 14A to 14B)`

-- s 14A(1), (2): Lena draws a Category A retirement pension; arguments: entitled to a pension or graduated benefit, pension deferred, graduated benefit deferred, day of payment, HMRC sent information, day it was sent.
-- Before the cut-off date (5 April 2017): 4 April yes, 5 April not "before".
#ASSERT `Under section 14A(1), may I pay a Class 3A contribution on this day` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 4 4 2017) FALSE (Date 1 1 2017) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 14A(1), may I pay a Class 3A contribution on this day` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 5 4 2017) FALSE (Date 1 1 2017) EQUALS NOTHING
-- HMRC sent information on 8 March 2017 in response to a request made before 6 April 2017: the 30-day period ends on 6 April 2017, so 5 April is before the cut-off; on 7 March it ends on 5 April.
#ASSERT `Under section 14A(1), may I pay a Class 3A contribution on this day` FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 5 4 2017) TRUE (Date 8 3 2017) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 14A(1), may I pay a Class 3A contribution on this day` FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 5 4 2017) TRUE (Date 7 3 2017) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not eligible: no pension, nothing deferred.
#ASSERT `Under section 14A(1), may I pay a Class 3A contribution on this day` FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 4 4 2017) FALSE (Date 1 1 2017) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 14A(5): arguments: paid before, units already obtained, units this payment would obtain, the maximum.
#ASSERT `Under section 14A(5), may I pay a Class 3A contribution on this occasion` TRUE 5 1 6 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 14A(5), may I pay a Class 3A contribution on this occasion` TRUE 5 2 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 14A(5), may I pay a Class 3A contribution on this occasion` FALSE 0 1 6 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 14A(5), may I pay a Class 3A contribution on this occasion` FALSE 0 7 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 14B(3): a repaid contribution means the unit is treated as never had.
#ASSERT `Under section 14B(3), am I treated as never having had the unit of additional pension` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 14B(3), am I treated as never having had the unit of additional pension` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Class 4 contributions on profits (ss 15 to 18A)`

-- s 15(1): Mo's profits are from a trade, chargeable under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005, and not from a trade wholly outside the United Kingdom.
#ASSERT `Under section 15(1), are Class 4 contributions payable on my profits for the tax year` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 15(1), are Class 4 contributions payable on my profits for the tax year` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 15(1), are Class 4 contributions payable on my profits for the tax year` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 15(3): nothing up to 12,570; 6% of the excess up to 50,270; 2% above it.
#ASSERT `Under section 15(3), how much Class 4 contribution must I pay on my profits for the tax year` TRUE TRUE FALSE 12570 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `Under section 15(3), how much Class 4 contribution must I pay on my profits for the tax year` TRUE TRUE FALSE 12670 EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `Under section 15(3), how much Class 4 contribution must I pay on my profits for the tax year` TRUE TRUE FALSE 50270 EQUALS JUST 2262
#ASSERT `Under section 15(3), how much Class 4 contribution must I pay on my profits for the tax year` TRUE TRUE FALSE 60000 EQUALS JUST 2456.6
