§§ `Contributions paid in error (s 19A)`

-- s 19A: Nia's employer paid Class 1 contributions for 2010-11 in error (her work was not employed earner's employment) and was not told of the error before the end of 2011-12. Arguments: year 1, paid in year 1, in error, payer notified, the day, prescribed exception, purpose.
-- Year 2 (2011-12) ends on 5 April 2012: from 6 April 2012 she is treated as in employed earner's employment for contributions and contributory benefits, and for sick pay and maternity pay.
#ASSERT `Under section 19A(2), am I treated as having been in employed earner's employment despite the error` 2010 TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 6 4 2012) FALSE `s 19A(2)(a) contributions and contributory benefits` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 19A(2), am I treated as having been in employed earner's employment despite the error` 2010 TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 6 4 2012) FALSE `s 19A(2)(b) statutory sick pay and statutory maternity pay` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 19A(2), am I treated as having been in employed earner's employment despite the error` 2010 TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 5 4 2012) FALSE `s 19A(2)(a) contributions and contributory benefits` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The payer was told of the error in time, a prescribed exception applies, the year is before 1998-99, or the purpose is another: not answered.
#ASSERT `Under section 19A(2), am I treated as having been in employed earner's employment despite the error` 2010 TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 6 4 2012) FALSE `s 19A(2)(a) contributions and contributory benefits` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 19A(2), am I treated as having been in employed earner's employment despite the error` 2010 TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 6 4 2012) TRUE `s 19A(2)(a) contributions and contributory benefits` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 19A(2), am I treated as having been in employed earner's employment despite the error` 1997 TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 6 4 2012) FALSE `s 19A(2)(a) contributions and contributory benefits` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 19A(2), am I treated as having been in employed earner's employment despite the error` 2010 TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 6 4 2012) FALSE `s 19A(2) another purpose` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part ssc2 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for the seat layer ssc2-seat.l4: every seat question is asked with the facts a real person in the
-- seat would state, and the answer is checked against an expected value written by hand from the text of the
-- Act (and the FALSE/NOTHING rule of the brief). Where a case has a note above it, the note gives the
-- derivation. Money figures are INVENTED test inputs: the rates and limits come from Schedule 4 and the
-- regulations, which are not in this text. The text is a converter rendering, not the official text.
--
-- A case that answers NOTHING asserts "not covered": the text is silent, limits itself in its own words, or
-- sends the answer outside Part II. It is never a "no".

§ `Cases -- ss 20 and 21: which benefits count, and the benefit year`
-- s 20(1) lists maternity allowance (d), short-term incapacity benefit (b)(i), widow's pension (e)(iii) and, for existing beneficiaries only, child's special allowance (g).
-- The list is open (fork F1): a benefit it does not name is not answered. "for existing beneficiaries only" closes (g): not an existing beneficiary is the text's own no.
#ASSERT `Under section 20(1), is the benefit I claim a contributory benefit under this Part` `maternity allowance` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(1), is the benefit I claim a contributory benefit under this Part` `short-term incapacity benefit` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(1), is the benefit I claim a contributory benefit under this Part` `widow's pension` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(1), is the benefit I claim a contributory benefit under this Part` `child's special allowance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(1), is the benefit I claim a contributory benefit under this Part` `child's special allowance` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(1), is the benefit I claim a contributory benefit under this Part` `attendance allowance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 20(2) defines "long-term benefit" and "short-term benefit" by "means": a benefit not in the definition is outside it (the text's own no).
#ASSERT `Under section 20(2), is the benefit I claim a long-term benefit` `long-term incapacity benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(2), is the benefit I claim a long-term benefit` `widowed parent's allowance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(2), is the benefit I claim a long-term benefit` `Category B retirement pension` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(2), is the benefit I claim a long-term benefit` `maternity allowance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(2), is the benefit I claim a short-term benefit` `short-term incapacity benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(2), is the benefit I claim a short-term benefit` `maternity allowance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(2), is the benefit I claim a short-term benefit` `long-term incapacity benefit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21(1): the requirement of contribution conditions applies to the benefits of s 20(1) other than the routes the section carves out ("other than" is the text's own no for those routes).
#ASSERT `Under section 21(1), does the requirement of contribution conditions apply to the benefit I claim` `short-term incapacity benefit` FALSE `s 21(1) any route not carved out` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 21(1), does the requirement of contribution conditions apply to the benefit I claim` `short-term incapacity benefit` FALSE `s 21(1) short-term incapacity benefit under section 30A(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 21(1), does the requirement of contribution conditions apply to the benefit I claim` `maternity allowance` FALSE `s 21(1) maternity allowance under section 35` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 21(1), does the requirement of contribution conditions apply to the benefit I claim` `shared additional pension` FALSE `s 21(1) shared additional pension under section 55A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 21(1), does the requirement of contribution conditions apply to the benefit I claim` `attendance allowance` FALSE `s 21(1) any route not carved out` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 21(1), does the requirement of contribution conditions apply to the benefit I claim` `widow's pension` FALSE `s 21(1) maternity allowance under section 35` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21(6): the benefit year begins with the first Sunday in January and ends on the Saturday before the first Sunday in January of the next year.
-- 1 January 2023 is a Sunday; 2024 begins on a Monday (first Sunday 7 January); 2025 on a Wednesday (first Sunday 5 January); 2026 on a Thursday (first Sunday 4 January).
#ASSERT (`Under section 21(6), when does the benefit year that begins in this calendar year start and end` 2023)'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 1 1 2023
#ASSERT (`Under section 21(6), when does the benefit year that begins in this calendar year start and end` 2023)'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 6 1 2024
#ASSERT (`Under section 21(6), when does the benefit year that begins in this calendar year start and end` 2024)'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 7 1 2024
#ASSERT (`Under section 21(6), when does the benefit year that begins in this calendar year start and end` 2024)'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 4 1 2025
#ASSERT (`Under section 21(6), when does the benefit year that begins in this calendar year start and end` 2025)'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 5 1 2025
#ASSERT (`Under section 21(6), when does the benefit year that begins in this calendar year start and end` 2025)'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 3 1 2026

