-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part ssc3 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for the seat layer ssc3-seat.l4: what a pensioner who states the facts below is told.
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section named beside it; none is copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each case names the facts as the person would state them, in the order the question asks them.
-- A "not covered" answer is NOTHING; a "no" the text gives in its own words is JUST FALSE (see NOTES.md, ### Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING).

§ `Section 43: more than one retirement pension`

-- (qualify A, rate A, qualify B, rate B, notice given, notice asks for A, date of notice, week begins)
-- s 43(5): no notice, so the most favourable pension: A at 100 beats B at 80.
#ASSERT `Under section 43, which retirement pension am I entitled to for a week when I qualify for both a Category A and a Category B pension` TRUE 100 TRUE 80 FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 8 1 2024) EQUALS JUST (LIST "my Category A pension")
-- s 43(5): B at 120 beats A at 100.
#ASSERT `Under section 43, which retirement pension am I entitled to for a week when I qualify for both a Category A and a Category B pension` TRUE 100 TRUE 120 FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 8 1 2024) EQUALS JUST (LIST "my Category B pension")
-- s 43(4): a notice dated 7 January asking for B governs a week commencing on 8 January, even though A is worth more.
#ASSERT `Under section 43, which retirement pension am I entitled to for a week when I qualify for both a Category A and a Category B pension` TRUE 100 TRUE 80 TRUE FALSE (Date 7 1 2024) (Date 8 1 2024) EQUALS JUST (LIST "my Category B pension")
-- s 43(4): "any week commencing after the date of the notice": a notice dated the day the week commences does not govern that week, so s 43(5) applies (reading F2 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `Under section 43, which retirement pension am I entitled to for a week when I qualify for both a Category A and a Category B pension` TRUE 100 TRUE 80 TRUE FALSE (Date 8 1 2024) (Date 8 1 2024) EQUALS JUST (LIST "my Category A pension")
-- s 43(4): a notice asking for A governs the week.
#ASSERT `Under section 43, which retirement pension am I entitled to for a week when I qualify for both a Category A and a Category B pension` TRUE 100 TRUE 120 TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 8 1 2024) EQUALS JUST (LIST "my Category A pension")
-- s 43(1): with one pension only there is nothing to choose.
#ASSERT `Under section 43, which retirement pension am I entitled to for a week when I qualify for both a Category A and a Category B pension` TRUE 100 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 8 1 2024) EQUALS JUST (LIST "my Category A pension")
#ASSERT `Under section 43, which retirement pension am I entitled to for a week when I qualify for both a Category A and a Category B pension` FALSE 0 TRUE 80 FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 8 1 2024) EQUALS JUST (LIST "my Category B pension")
-- s 43(1): with no pension there is none to name.
#ASSERT `Under section 43, which retirement pension am I entitled to for a week when I qualify for both a Category A and a Category B pension` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 8 1 2024) EQUALS JUST EMPTY

§ `Section 44: Category A retirement pension`

-- (day I attain pensionable age, contributions satisfy the conditions)
-- s 44(1): attained before 6 April 2016 and the contribution conditions satisfied.
#ASSERT `Under section 44(1), am I entitled to a Category A retirement pension` (Date 9 3 2012) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 44(1): "if" the conditions are satisfied; they are not (reading (a): a failed "if" is the text's no).
#ASSERT `Under section 44(1), am I entitled to a Category A retirement pension` (Date 9 3 2012) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 44(1)(a): 5 April 2016 is before 6 April 2016; 6 April 2016 is not.
#ASSERT `Under section 44(1), am I entitled to a Category A retirement pension` (Date 5 4 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 44(1), am I entitled to a Category A retirement pension` (Date 6 4 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 44(1) closing words: entitled on the day of attaining pensionable age.
#ASSERT `Under section 44(1), on what day do I become entitled to a Category A retirement pension` (Date 9 3 2012) EQUALS Date 9 3 2012
-- (day I attain, contributions, day I ask about, I have died, day I died)
-- s 44(1) closing words: running from the day of attaining pensionable age, throughout life.
#ASSERT `Under section 44(1), is my Category A retirement pension running on a given day` (Date 9 3 2012) TRUE (Date 9 3 2012) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 44(1), is my Category A retirement pension running on a given day` (Date 9 3 2012) TRUE (Date 1 1 2040) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not covered: a day before the person attained pensionable age (the text says when entitlement begins, and says nothing of earlier days).
#ASSERT `Under section 44(1), is my Category A retirement pension running on a given day` (Date 9 3 2012) TRUE (Date 8 3 2012) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The day of death is within "throughout his life"; the day after is not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 44(1), is my Category A retirement pension running on a given day` (Date 9 3 2012) TRUE (Date 1 1 2030) TRUE (Date 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 44(1), is my Category A retirement pension running on a given day` (Date 9 3 2012) TRUE (Date 2 1 2030) TRUE (Date 1 1 2030) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Inheriting s 44(1)'s no: the conditions are not satisfied, so there is no entitlement to run.
#ASSERT `Under section 44(1), is my Category A retirement pension running on a given day` (Date 9 3 2012) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (day I ask about, day my entitlement is regarded as commencing under section 5(1)(k))
-- s 44(2): a day before the day on which the entitlement is regarded as commencing is not a day for which the pension is payable.
#ASSERT `Under section 44(2), is my Category A retirement pension payable in respect of a given day` (Date 9 3 2012) (Date 10 3 2012) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: from the commencing day on, the text says nothing of whether the pension is payable.
#ASSERT `Under section 44(2), is my Category A retirement pension payable in respect of a given day` (Date 10 3 2012) (Date 10 3 2012) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 44(4): the basic pension is 184.90 a week, or 140.65 where the sum is for the lower rate of short-term incapacity benefit.
#ASSERT `Under section 44(4), what is the weekly rate of my basic pension` FALSE EQUALS JUST 184.9
#ASSERT `Under section 44(4), what is the weekly rate of my basic pension` TRUE EQUALS JUST 140.65

§ `Sections 44A to 44C: earnings factors for a year or a week`

-- (earnings factor, qualifying earnings factor, low earnings threshold, carer's allowance throughout, carer's allowance would have been, child benefit throughout, child under 6, other prescribed, LTIB throughout, failed contribution conditions, reduced to nil by other benefits, reduced to nil by scheme, occupational scheme, personal scheme, working life before exclusions, before 1978-79, treated by (b) or (c), years with factor at least QEF, other earnings factors)
-- s 44A(2)(a): 8000 lies from the qualifying earnings factor (5000) up to the low earnings threshold (9500), so the deemed factor brings the total to 9500: 1500 more.
#ASSERT `Under section 44A, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year in which my own earnings factor was low` 8000 5000 9500 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 40 0 0 0 8000 EQUALS JUST 1500
-- s 44A(2)(b): carer's allowance throughout the year, with an earnings factor of 1000 (below the qualifying earnings factor): 9500 less 1000.
#ASSERT `Under section 44A, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year in which my own earnings factor was low` 1000 5000 9500 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 40 0 0 0 1000 EQUALS JUST 8500
-- s 44A(2)(d) with (3): long-term incapacity benefit throughout the year, and 4 relevant years at or above the qualifying earnings factor against one tenth of a 40-year working life (4).
#ASSERT `Under section 44A, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year in which my own earnings factor was low` 1000 5000 9500 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 40 0 0 4 1000 EQUALS JUST 8500
-- Not covered: with 3 such years, below one tenth of the working life, none of the four conditions holds and the text gives no deemed factor.
#ASSERT `Under section 44A, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year in which my own earnings factor was low` 1000 5000 9500 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 40 0 0 3 1000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: an earnings factor of 4000 is below the qualifying earnings factor and no other condition holds.
#ASSERT `Under section 44A, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year in which my own earnings factor was low` 4000 5000 9500 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 40 0 0 0 4000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (earnings factor apart from 44B, apart from 44B and 44C, qualifying earnings factor, low earnings threshold, aggregate of credits, number of credits, flat rate year or later, other earnings factors)
-- s 44B(3) Condition A: 6000 lies from 5000 up to, but not including, 9500: deemed factor 9500 less 6000.
#ASSERT `Under section 44B, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year from the flat rate introduction year` 6000 6000 5000 9500 0 0 FALSE 6000 EQUALS JUST 3500
-- s 44B(5) Condition C: 52 credits.
#ASSERT `Under section 44B, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year from the flat rate introduction year` 3000 3000 5000 9500 100 52 FALSE 3000 EQUALS JUST 6500
-- s 44B(4) Condition B: below the qualifying earnings factor, with credits that make up exactly the difference (2000).
#ASSERT `Under section 44B, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year from the flat rate introduction year` 3000 3000 5000 9500 2000 10 FALSE 3000 EQUALS JUST 6500
-- Not covered: no condition holds.
#ASSERT `Under section 44B, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year from the flat rate introduction year` 3000 3000 5000 9500 0 0 FALSE 3000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: from the flat rate introduction year s 44B(6)(a) names a range (more than the qualifying earnings factor, less than the low earnings threshold) and no amount (fork F4 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `Under section 44B, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year from the flat rate introduction year` 6000 6000 5000 9500 0 0 TRUE 6000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (week in a relevant year, relevant carer, carer's allowance part of week, would have been, SDA, LTIB, failed contribution conditions, reduced by other benefits, reduced by scheme, occupational, personal, other prescribed, qualifying earnings factor)
-- s 44C(2): a credit of 1/52 of the qualifying earnings factor (5200) for a week in which the person was a relevant carer.
#ASSERT `Under section 44C, what earnings factor credit do I get for a week` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 5200 EQUALS JUST 100
-- s 44C(3): carer's allowance payable for part of the week is enough.
#ASSERT `Under section 44C, what earnings factor credit do I get for a week` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 5200 EQUALS JUST 100
-- Not covered: no condition of s 44C(3) holds for the week.
#ASSERT `Under section 44C, what earnings factor credit do I get for a week` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 5200 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: the week is not in a relevant year to which s 44C applies.
#ASSERT `Under section 44C, what earnings factor credit do I get for a week` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 5200 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 45 to 45B: additional pension`

-- (day I attain pensionable age, adjusted surpluses, units, specified amount for each unit)
-- s 45(1): 1.25 per cent of 10400 is 130 a year, 2.50 a week; no units.
#ASSERT `Under section 45(1), what is the weekly rate of my additional pension if I reached pensionable age before 6 April 1999` (Date 5 4 1999) 10400 0 0 EQUALS JUST 2.5
-- s 45(1): plus 2 units at 3.10 each.
#ASSERT `Under section 45(1), what is the weekly rate of my additional pension if I reached pensionable age before 6 April 1999` (Date 5 4 1999) 10400 2 3.1 EQUALS JUST 8.7
-- Not covered: subsection (1) speaks of a pensioner who attained pensionable age before 6 April 1999.
#ASSERT `Under section 45(1), what is the weekly rate of my additional pension if I reached pensionable age before 6 April 1999` (Date 6 4 1999) 10400 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (day I attain pensionable age, surpluses 1978-79 to 1987-88, surpluses after 1987-88, N, Schedule 4A amount, Schedule 4B amount, section 39C calculation, deceased under pensionable age, units, specified amount)
-- s 45(2): attained in June 2012; the four amounts and the units add to 39 a week.
#ASSERT `Under section 45(2), what is the weekly rate of my additional pension if I reached pensionable age on or after 6 April 1999` (Date 1 6 2012) 15600 31200 30 520 1040 FALSE FALSE 1 2.5 EQUALS JUST 39
-- s 46(4)(a): in a bereavement case under s 39C where the person who died was under pensionable age, paragraph (d) (the Schedule 4B amount) is omitted: 39 less 20 is 19.
#ASSERT `Under section 45(2), what is the weekly rate of my additional pension if I reached pensionable age on or after 6 April 1999` (Date 1 6 2012) 15600 31200 30 520 1040 TRUE TRUE 1 2.5 EQUALS JUST 19
-- s 46(4) is limited to a death under pensionable age: the person who died was not, so paragraph (d) stays.
#ASSERT `Under section 45(2), what is the weekly rate of my additional pension if I reached pensionable age on or after 6 April 1999` (Date 1 6 2012) 15600 31200 30 520 1040 TRUE FALSE 1 2.5 EQUALS JUST 39
-- Not covered: attained on 5 April 1999, which subsection (2) does not reach.
#ASSERT `Under section 45(2), what is the weekly rate of my additional pension if I reached pensionable age on or after 6 April 1999` (Date 5 4 1999) 15600 31200 30 520 1040 FALSE FALSE 1 2.5 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (weekly rate before the reduction, appropriate weekly amount, in or after the final relevant year, relevant revaluation percentage)
-- s 45B(2)/(3): in or after the final relevant year the reduction is the appropriate weekly amount, 100 less 20.
#ASSERT `Under section 45B, what is the weekly rate of my additional pension after a pension debit` 100 20 TRUE 150 EQUALS JUST 80
-- s 45B(3): before the final relevant year the amount is revalued by 150 per cent: 100 less 30.
#ASSERT `Under section 45B, what is the weekly rate of my additional pension after a pension debit` 100 20 FALSE 150 EQUALS JUST 70
-- Not covered: a revalued reduction of 120 exceeds the rate of 100, and the text sets no floor.
#ASSERT `Under section 45B, what is the weekly rate of my additional pension after a pension debit` 100 80 FALSE 150 EQUALS NOTHING

-- (a tax credit was paid, unrevoked reduced-rate election, earnings on which contributions were paid, qualifying earnings factor, AG, upper earnings limit)
-- s 45AA(1)(a): earnings of 8000 are not less than the qualifying earnings factor (6000), so they are increased by AG (500).
#ASSERT `Under section 45AA, what are my qualifying earnings for a year in which a tax credit was paid` TRUE FALSE 8000 6000 500 40000 EQUALS JUST 8500
-- s 45AA(1)(b): earnings of 3000 are below the factor (6000), so the qualifying earnings are AG plus the factor.
#ASSERT `Under section 45AA, what are my qualifying earnings for a year in which a tax credit was paid` TRUE FALSE 3000 6000 500 40000 EQUALS JUST 6500
-- s 45AA(3): the figure (8500) cannot exceed the upper earnings limit (100) multiplied by 53, which is 5300.
#ASSERT `Under section 45AA, what are my qualifying earnings for a year in which a tax credit was paid` TRUE FALSE 8000 6000 500 100 EQUALS JUST 5300
-- Not covered: s 45AA(4) says subsection (1) does not apply to a woman with an unrevoked reduced-rate election, and the section gives no figure.
#ASSERT `Under section 45AA, what are my qualifying earnings for a year in which a tax credit was paid` TRUE TRUE 8000 6000 500 40000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: no tax credit was paid, so s 45AA(1) does not operate.
#ASSERT `Under section 45AA, what are my qualifying earnings for a year in which a tax credit was paid` FALSE FALSE 8000 6000 500 40000 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 47: increase for a long-term incapacity age addition`

-- (age addition on a day in the 8 weeks, age addition on the last day before them, rate of the age addition, payable only by virtue of s 60(1), no basic pension)
-- s 47(1)(a): entitled on a day in the 8 weeks, so the weekly rate is increased by the age addition (5.75).
#ASSERT `Under section 47(1), by how much is my Category A pension increased because I got an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit` TRUE FALSE 5.75 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 5.75
-- s 47(1)(b): entitled on the last day before the 8 weeks.
#ASSERT `Under section 47(1), by how much is my Category A pension increased because I got an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit` FALSE TRUE 5.75 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 5.75
-- s 47(1): "if the pensioner was entitled": neither day (reading (a)), so no increase.
#ASSERT `Under section 47(1), by how much is my Category A pension increased because I got an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit` FALSE FALSE 5.75 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- s 61(1): a pension payable by virtue of s 60(1) with no basic pension "shall not be increased under section 47(1)".
#ASSERT `Under section 47(1), by how much is my Category A pension increased because I got an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit` TRUE FALSE 5.75 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `Under section 47(1), by how much is my Category A pension increased because I got an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit` TRUE FALSE 5.75 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 5.75

§ `Sections 48 to 48BB: Category A or B pension from another person's contributions`

-- (day I attain pensionable age, relevant relationship, day it ended, last relevant relationship, own contributions satisfy, claim for Category A)
-- s 48(1): a person who attained pensionable age on 5 April 2016, whose own contributions fall short, and whose last relationship ended in 2000.
#ASSERT `Under section 48(1), can my former spouse's or civil partner's contributions be treated as my own for a Category A retirement pension` (Date 5 4 2016) TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 48(1)(b): their own contributions satisfy the conditions, so there is no need.
#ASSERT `Under section 48(1), can my former spouse's or civil partner's contributions be treated as my own for a Category A retirement pension` (Date 5 4 2016) TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48(1): "before 6 April 2016": 6 April 2016 is too late.
#ASSERT `Under section 48(1), can my former spouse's or civil partner's contributions be treated as my own for a Category A retirement pension` (Date 6 4 2016) TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48(1): "only in respect of any claim for a Category A retirement pension".
#ASSERT `Under section 48(1), can my former spouse's or civil partner's contributions be treated as my own for a Category A retirement pension` (Date 5 4 2016) TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48(3): "applies only to the last relevant relationship".
#ASSERT `Under section 48(1), can my former spouse's or civil partner's contributions be treated as my own for a Category A retirement pension` (Date 5 4 2016) TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48(2): attained pensionable age before 6 April 1979 and the relationship also ended before that date.
#ASSERT `Under section 48(1), can my former spouse's or civil partner's contributions be treated as my own for a Category A retirement pension` (Date 1 1 1978) TRUE (Date 1 1 1978) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (I am a woman, day I attain, married to spouse, spouse is a woman, spouse's date of birth, day spouse attains, day I ask about, spouse is a woman by gender recognition, marriage subsisted before it, spouse's contributions satisfy)
-- s 48A(1): a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2013, married to a man born on 6 April 1950 who attained it on 1 January 2015, asking about 1 January 2020.
#ASSERT `Under section 48A(1), am I, as a married person, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my spouse's contributions` TRUE (Date 1 1 2013) TRUE FALSE (Date 6 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 48A(1), am I, as a married person, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my spouse's contributions` TRUE (Date 1 1 2013) TRUE FALSE (Date 6 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48A(1)(b)(i): the spouse has not yet attained pensionable age on 31 December 2014.
#ASSERT `Under section 48A(1), am I, as a married person, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my spouse's contributions` TRUE (Date 1 1 2013) TRUE FALSE (Date 6 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 31 12 2014) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48A(2)(a): "a man whose spouse was born before 6 April 1950".
#ASSERT `Under section 48A(1), am I, as a married person, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my spouse's contributions` FALSE (Date 1 1 2013) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 1949) (Date 1 1 2009) (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48A(2)(b): "a woman whose wife was born before 6 April 1950"; s 51ZA(1) lifts it where she is a woman by a gender recognition certificate and the marriage predates it.
#ASSERT `Under section 48A(1), am I, as a married person, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my spouse's contributions` TRUE (Date 1 1 2013) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 1949) (Date 1 1 2009) (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 48A(1), am I, as a married person, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my spouse's contributions` TRUE (Date 1 1 2013) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 1949) (Date 1 1 2009) (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (day I attain, civil partner of the contributing partner, partner's date of birth, day partner attains, day I ask about, partner's contributions satisfy)
-- s 48A(3): the contributing civil partner was born on 6 April 1950 (on or after it) and attained pensionable age on 1 January 2015.
