-- s 48A(3)(b)(i): born on 5 April 1950 is before the date the paragraph names.
#ASSERT `Under section 48A(3), am I, as a civil partner, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my civil partner's contributions` (Date 1 1 2013) TRUE (Date 5 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 48A(3), am I, as a civil partner, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my civil partner's contributions` (Date 1 1 2013) TRUE (Date 6 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 31 12 2014) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 48A(3), am I, as a civil partner, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my civil partner's contributions` (Date 1 1 2013) TRUE (Date 6 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (I am a woman, day I attain, former spouse is a woman, former spouse's date of birth, day former spouse attains, day dissolved, gender recognition, marriage subsisted, former spouse's contributions satisfy)
-- s 48AA(1): marriage dissolved on 1 January 2018, after the former spouse attained pensionable age (1 January 2015).
#ASSERT `Under section 48AA(1), am I, after a divorce, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my former spouse's contributions` TRUE (Date 1 1 2013) FALSE (Date 6 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2018) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 48AA(1), am I, after a divorce, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my former spouse's contributions` TRUE (Date 1 1 2013) FALSE (Date 6 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2018) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 48AA(1), am I, after a divorce, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my former spouse's contributions` TRUE (Date 1 1 2013) FALSE (Date 6 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2014) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (I am a woman, day I attain, late spouse is a woman, late spouse's date of birth, day late spouse attained, day spouse died, died while married, gender recognition, marriage subsisted, late spouse's contributions satisfy)
-- s 48B(1): the spouse died on 1 January 2017, while married; the person attained pensionable age on 1 January 2013, before the death.
#ASSERT `Under section 48B(1), am I, as a widow or widower, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my late spouse's contributions` TRUE (Date 1 1 2013) FALSE (Date 6 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2017) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 48B(1), am I, as a widow or widower, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my late spouse's contributions` TRUE (Date 1 1 2013) FALSE (Date 6 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2017) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48B(1): "whose spouse died while they were married": not married at death.
#ASSERT `Under section 48B(1), am I, as a widow or widower, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my late spouse's contributions` TRUE (Date 1 1 2013) FALSE (Date 6 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2017) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48B(1): the spouse died on the day the person attained pensionable age, not after it.
#ASSERT `Under section 48B(1), am I, as a widow or widower, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my late spouse's contributions` TRUE (Date 1 1 2013) FALSE (Date 6 4 1950) (Date 1 1 2015) (Date 1 1 2013) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (day I attain, deceased's date of birth, day deceased attained, day civil partner died, died while civil partners, deceased's contributions satisfy)
-- s 48B(1A): a civil partner who attained pensionable age on 6 April 2010, whose civil partner (born 1 January 1944) died on 1 January 2012.
#ASSERT `Under section 48B(1A), am I, as a surviving civil partner, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my late civil partner's contributions` (Date 6 4 2010) (Date 1 1 1944) (Date 1 1 2009) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 48B(1A), am I, as a surviving civil partner, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my late civil partner's contributions` (Date 6 4 2010) (Date 1 1 1944) (Date 1 1 2009) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48B(1A)(a): attained pensionable age on 5 April 2010, before the date the paragraph names.
#ASSERT `Under section 48B(1A), am I, as a surviving civil partner, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my late civil partner's contributions` (Date 5 4 2010) (Date 1 1 1944) (Date 1 1 2009) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (additional pension as for Category A, day spouse died)
-- s 48B(2): the basic pension (184.90) plus half the additional pension (20), the spouse having died after 5 October 2002.
#ASSERT `Under section 48B(2), what is the weekly rate of my Category B retirement pension` 20 (Date 6 10 2002) EQUALS JUST 194.9
-- s 48C(3): the spouse died on 5 October 2002, so "half of" is omitted: 184.90 plus 20.
#ASSERT `Under section 48B(2), what is the weekly rate of my Category B retirement pension` 20 (Date 5 10 2002) EQUALS JUST 204.9
-- (bereavement allowance before pensionable age, widowed parent's allowance at some time, over 45 then, widowed parent's allowance immediately before pensionable age, not since married)
-- s 48BB(4): a bereavement allowance before pensionable age (attained 1 January 2013), and no remarriage.
#ASSERT `Under section 48BB(4), am I entitled to a Category B retirement pension on the contributions of my late spouse or civil partner after getting bereavement allowance or widowed parent's allowance` (Date 1 1 2013) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 48BB(4): a widowed parent's allowance at some time when over 45, not still getting it at pensionable age, no remarriage.
#ASSERT `Under section 48BB(4), am I entitled to a Category B retirement pension on the contributions of my late spouse or civil partner after getting bereavement allowance or widowed parent's allowance` (Date 1 1 2013) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 48BB(4), am I entitled to a Category B retirement pension on the contributions of my late spouse or civil partner after getting bereavement allowance or widowed parent's allowance` (Date 1 1 2013) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 48BB(4), am I entitled to a Category B retirement pension on the contributions of my late spouse or civil partner after getting bereavement allowance or widowed parent's allowance` (Date 1 1 2013) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48BB(4): remarried since the death.
#ASSERT `Under section 48BB(4), am I entitled to a Category B retirement pension on the contributions of my late spouse or civil partner after getting bereavement allowance or widowed parent's allowance` (Date 1 1 2013) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 48BB(4): attained pensionable age on 6 April 2016, not before it.
#ASSERT `Under section 48BB(4), am I entitled to a Category B retirement pension on the contributions of my late spouse or civil partner after getting bereavement allowance or widowed parent's allowance` (Date 6 4 2016) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Sections 51 and 52: widow or widower, and the increase to a Category A pension`

-- (I am a woman, day I attain, late spouse is a woman, day late spouse attained, day spouse died, died while married, gender recognition, marriage subsisted, late spouse's contributions satisfy)
-- s 51(1): a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005, whose wife (attained 1 January 2004) died on 1 January 2008 while they were married.
#ASSERT `Under section 51(1), am I, as a widow or widower, entitled to a Category B retirement pension` FALSE (Date 1 1 2005) TRUE (Date 1 1 2004) (Date 1 1 2008) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 51(1), am I, as a widow or widower, entitled to a Category B retirement pension` FALSE (Date 1 1 2005) TRUE (Date 1 1 2004) (Date 1 1 2008) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 51(1): the spouse died before the person attained pensionable age (31 December 2004 against 1 January 2005).
#ASSERT `Under section 51(1), am I, as a widow or widower, entitled to a Category B retirement pension` FALSE (Date 1 1 2005) TRUE (Date 1 1 2004) (Date 31 12 2004) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 51(1): the person attained pensionable age on the day the spouse died.
#ASSERT `Under section 51(1), am I, as a widow or widower, entitled to a Category B retirement pension` FALSE (Date 1 1 2005) TRUE (Date 1 1 2004) (Date 1 1 2005) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (day spouse died, day I attain, apart from s 43(1) entitled to A, apart from s 43(1) entitled to B, Category A basic falls short, basic pension in A, basic pension in B)
-- s 52(2): the shortfall (184.90 less 100) is 84.90, but the increase is limited to the amount of basic pension in the Category B rate (30).
#ASSERT `Under section 52(2), by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because I am a surviving spouse` (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 1 1985) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 30 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `Under section 52(2), by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because I am a surviving spouse` (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 1 1985) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 100 EQUALS JUST 84.9
#ASSERT `Under section 52(2), by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because I am a surviving spouse` (Date 1 1 1990) (Date 1 1 1985) TRUE TRUE FALSE 100 100 EQUALS JUST 0

-- (day I attain, day the other party attains, apart from s 43(1) entitled to A, apart from s 43(1) entitled to B on the other party's contributions, A falls short by a deficiency of contributions, basic pension in A, Schedule 4 Part I para 5 rate, basic pension in the B rate)
-- s 51A(2): the shortfall (150 less 100) is 50, but the increase is limited to the basic pension in the Category B rate (30).
#ASSERT `Under section 51A, by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because of my spouse's or civil partner's contributions` (Date 1 1 1985) (Date 1 1 1990) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 150 30 EQUALS JUST 30
-- s 51A(2): the shortfall (50) is the lesser of 50 and 60.
#ASSERT `Under section 51A, by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because of my spouse's or civil partner's contributions` (Date 1 1 1985) (Date 1 1 1990) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 150 60 EQUALS JUST 50
-- s 51A(2): a basic pension equal to the Schedule 4 rate does not fall short of it.
#ASSERT `Under section 51A, by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because of my spouse's or civil partner's contributions` (Date 1 1 1985) (Date 1 1 1990) TRUE TRUE TRUE 150 150 30 EQUALS JUST 0
-- s 51A(2): the basic pension does not fall short by reason of a deficiency of contributions.
#ASSERT `Under section 51A, by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because of my spouse's or civil partner's contributions` (Date 1 1 1985) (Date 1 1 1990) TRUE TRUE FALSE 100 150 30 EQUALS JUST 0
-- s 51A(1): apart from s 43(1) the person would not be entitled to a Category B pension on the other party's contributions.
#ASSERT `Under section 51A, by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because of my spouse's or civil partner's contributions` (Date 1 1 1985) (Date 1 1 1990) TRUE FALSE TRUE 100 150 30 EQUALS JUST 0
-- s 51A(3): both parties attained pensionable age before 6 April 1979, so the section does not apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 51A, by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because of my spouse's or civil partner's contributions` (Date 1 1 1970) (Date 1 1 1975) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 150 30 EQUALS JUST 0
-- s 51A(3): both attained it on 5 April 1979, the day before the cut-off, so the section does not apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 51A, by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because of my spouse's or civil partner's contributions` (Date 5 4 1979) (Date 5 4 1979) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 150 30 EQUALS JUST 0
-- s 51A(3): one of the two attained it on 6 April 1979, so not both attained it before that day and the section applies.
#ASSERT `Under section 51A, by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because of my spouse's or civil partner's contributions` (Date 5 4 1979) (Date 6 4 1979) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 150 30 EQUALS JUST 30

§ `Section 55: deferment`

-- (not yet entitled only because no claim, elected under section 54(1))
-- s 55(3): deferred where the person does not become entitled only for want of a claim, or because of an election.
#ASSERT `Under section 55(3), is my retirement pension deferred` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 55(3), is my retirement pension deferred` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 55(3), is my retirement pension deferred` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Sections 55A to 55C: shared additional pension`

-- (day I attain, entitled to an old state scheme pension credit)
-- s 55A(1): attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and entitled to the credit.
#ASSERT `Under section 55A(1), am I entitled to a shared additional pension because of an old state scheme pension credit` (Date 5 4 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 55A(1), am I entitled to a shared additional pension because of an old state scheme pension credit` (Date 6 4 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 55A(1), am I entitled to a shared additional pension because of an old state scheme pension credit` (Date 5 4 2016) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (day I attain, day entitlement to the credit arose, appropriate weekly amount, revaluation percentage)
-- s 55A(3): an entitlement arising before the final relevant year (a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012; the year before is 2010-11) is revalued by 110 per cent: 20 becomes 22.
#ASSERT `Under section 55A(3), what is the weekly rate of my shared additional pension` (Date 1 1 2012) (Date 5 4 2010) 20 110 EQUALS JUST 22
-- s 55A(3): an entitlement arising on 6 April 2010 is in the final relevant year: not revalued.
#ASSERT `Under section 55A(3), what is the weekly rate of my shared additional pension` (Date 1 1 2012) (Date 6 4 2010) 20 110 EQUALS JUST 20
-- (day I attain, entitled to a new state scheme pension credit)
#ASSERT `Under section 55AA(1), am I entitled to a shared additional pension because of a new state scheme pension credit` (Date 5 4 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 55AA(1), am I entitled to a shared additional pension because of a new state scheme pension credit` (Date 6 4 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 55AA(3): the weekly rate is the amount of the credit.
#ASSERT `Under section 55AA(3), what is the weekly rate of my shared additional pension` 30 EQUALS JUST 30
-- (day I attain, subject to a debit, referable to the shared additional pension, day subject to the debit, rate before the reduction, appropriate weekly amount, revaluation percentage)
-- s 55B(1)-(3): a debit from 6 April 2010 (a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012): 50 less 8.
#ASSERT `Under section 55B, what is the weekly rate of my shared additional pension after a pension debit` (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE TRUE (Date 6 4 2010) 50 8 110 EQUALS JUST 42
-- s 55B(3): a debit from 5 April 2010 is revalued by 110 per cent: 8 becomes 8.80, and 50 less 8.80 is 41.20.
#ASSERT `Under section 55B, what is the weekly rate of my shared additional pension after a pension debit` (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE TRUE (Date 5 4 2010) 50 8 110 EQUALS JUST 41.2
-- s 55B(1): no reduction where the debit is not referable to the shared additional pension.
#ASSERT `Under section 55B, what is the weekly rate of my shared additional pension after a pension debit` (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE FALSE (Date 6 4 2010) 50 8 110 EQUALS JUST 50
-- (would be entitled but for deferral, retirement pension not entitled only for want of a claim, elected, shared additional pension not entitled only for want of a claim)
-- s 55C(3): the retirement pension is deferred for want of a claim and the shared additional pension likewise.
#ASSERT `Under section 55C(3), is my shared additional pension deferred` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 55C(3), is my shared additional pension deferred` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 55C(3), is my shared additional pension deferred` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 56: child's special allowance`

-- (divorced, husband dead, husband satisfied the contribution condition, entitled to child benefit, so entitled immediately before his death, in the prescribed circumstances so entitled, he had been contributing, court order, after remarriage, living with a man, entitled apart from (3), Part IX living with me, rate I contribute, one of two spouses, rate together, amount in (3), prescribed case, over and above, 1987 conditions, 1987 not barred, continued since, day)
-- s 56(1): all eight conditions hold; no bar applies; she satisfied the s 56(6) saving conditions immediately before 6 April 1987 and since.
#ASSERT `Under section 56(1), is the child's special allowance payable to me for a day` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 10 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 56(2): the period is after her remarriage.
#ASSERT `Under section 56(1), is the child's special allowance payable to me for a day` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 10 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 56(2): during the period she lives with a man as husband and wife.
#ASSERT `Under section 56(1), is the child's special allowance payable to me for a day` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 10 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 56(1): the marriage was not terminated by divorce.
#ASSERT `Under section 56(1), is the child's special allowance payable to me for a day` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 10 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 56(3): the amount "shall not be payable unless one of the conditions specified in subsection (4) is satisfied": entitled apart from the subsection, and the child is treated under Part IX as living with her (4)(a), so it is payable.
#ASSERT `Under section 56(1), is the child's special allowance payable to me for a day` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE 0 10 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 56(4)(b) and (5): contributions of 10 a week reach the amount in subsection (3) (10) and are over and above those needed for s 143(1)(b), so the condition is satisfied and it is payable.
#ASSERT `Under section 56(1), is the child's special allowance payable to me for a day` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 10 FALSE 0 10 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 56(3): contributions of 9 fall short of the amount in subsection (3) (10), she is not treated as having the child living with her, and no condition in subsection (4) is satisfied, so the amount is not payable.
#ASSERT `Under section 56(1), is the child's special allowance payable to me for a day` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 9 FALSE 15 10 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 56(6): did not satisfy the conditions immediately before 6 April 1987, so payment is barred.
#ASSERT `Under section 56(1), is the child's special allowance payable to me for a day` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 56(1) rate: Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 6 sets it; the person states it.
#ASSERT `Under section 56(1), what is the weekly rate of my child's special allowance` 17.5 EQUALS JUST 17.5

§ `Sections 60 to 62: contribution failures, units of additional pension, gender change`

-- (day the employed earner died, married or a civil partner, s 94(1) injury, s 108(1) disease, conditions not wholly satisfied, Category B pension under 48B or 48BB, paragraph 5A applies)
-- s 60(2): a death on 11 April 1988 (the first day on which it has effect) of a person in an injury within s 94(1).
#ASSERT `Under section 60(2), are the contribution conditions taken to be satisfied for my Category B retirement pension, because my spouse or civil partner died of an industrial injury or disease` (Date 11 4 1988) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 60(2), are the contribution conditions taken to be satisfied for my Category B retirement pension, because my spouse or civil partner died of an industrial injury or disease` (Date 11 4 1988) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 60(8): a death on 10 April 1988 is before the date the subsection names.
#ASSERT `Under section 60(2), are the contribution conditions taken to be satisfied for my Category B retirement pension, because my spouse or civil partner died of an industrial injury or disease` (Date 10 4 1988) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 60(2): neither the s 94(1) injury nor the s 108(1) disease.
#ASSERT `Under section 60(2), are the contribution conditions taken to be satisfied for my Category B retirement pension, because my spouse or civil partner died of an industrial injury or disease` (Date 11 4 1988) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 60(3): the pension is not a Category B pension payable under s 48B or 48BB.
#ASSERT `Under section 60(2), are the contribution conditions taken to be satisfied for my Category B retirement pension, because my spouse or civil partner died of an industrial injury or disease` (Date 11 4 1988) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5A(4) modifies the condition, condition as modified satisfied, condition as unmodified satisfied, benefit is one to which 5A applies, would have been entitled, years that satisfy 5A(2)(a) and (b), prescribed proportion for each year)
-- s 60A(2): the condition is not satisfied, the person would have been entitled had it been, and 12 years of the working life satisfy the requirements: 12 times the prescribed proportion (0.01).
#ASSERT `Under section 60A, what proportion of my benefit am I entitled to although the paragraph 5A contribution condition is not satisfied` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 12 0.01 EQUALS JUST 0.12
-- s 60A(6): the condition includes the condition as modified by paragraph 5A(4); modified, it is satisfied, so subsection (2) does not apply and there is no proportion to add.
#ASSERT `Under section 60A, what proportion of my benefit am I entitled to although the paragraph 5A contribution condition is not satisfied` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 12 0.01 EQUALS JUST 0
-- s 60A(1): the condition is satisfied without modification, so subsection (2) applies "if the contribution condition ... is not satisfied" and does not here.
#ASSERT `Under section 60A, what proportion of my benefit am I entitled to although the paragraph 5A contribution condition is not satisfied` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 12 0.01 EQUALS JUST 0
-- s 60A(2): a person who would not have been entitled had the condition been satisfied gets no proportion.
#ASSERT `Under section 60A, what proportion of my benefit am I entitled to although the paragraph 5A contribution condition is not satisfied` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 12 0.01 EQUALS JUST 0
-- (units of additional pension, entitled to a Category A pension, would be entitled if the conditions were satisfied)
-- s 61ZA(1)/(2): units of additional pension, not otherwise entitled, but would be entitled if the conditions were satisfied.
#ASSERT `Under section 61ZA, are the contribution conditions for my Category A retirement pension taken to be satisfied because of my units of additional pension` 2 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not covered: no units of additional pension, so s 61ZA(1) does not apply and s 61ZA(2) says nothing.
#ASSERT `Under section 61ZA, are the contribution conditions for my Category A retirement pension taken to be satisfied because of my units of additional pension` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: already entitled, so s 61ZA(1) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 61ZA, are the contribution conditions for my Category A retirement pension taken to be satisfied because of my units of additional pension` 2 TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (units of additional pension my late spouse had, entitled to a Category B pension as a result of the death, would be entitled if the conditions were satisfied)
-- s 61ZB(1)/(2): a dead spouse with units of additional pension, a person not otherwise entitled who would be if the conditions were satisfied.
#ASSERT `Under section 61ZB, are the contribution conditions for my Category B retirement pension taken to be satisfied because of my late spouse's or civil partner's units of additional pension` 3 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not covered: no units of additional pension, so s 61ZB(1) does not apply and s 61ZB(2) says nothing.
#ASSERT `Under section 61ZB, are the contribution conditions for my Category B retirement pension taken to be satisfied because of my late spouse's or civil partner's units of additional pension` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: already entitled to the Category B pension as a result of the death.
#ASSERT `Under section 61ZB, are the contribution conditions for my Category B retirement pension taken to be satisfied because of my late spouse's or civil partner's units of additional pension` 3 TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (I have a Category A pension because of s 61ZA, number of Category B pensions I have)
-- s 61ZC(1): a Category A pension because of s 61ZA together with one Category B pension; section 43 does not prevent both, so yes, they may.
#ASSERT `Under section 61ZC(1), may I have both a Category A retirement pension because of units of additional pension and a Category B retirement pension, despite section 43` TRUE 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 61ZC(1): "one Category B retirement pension (or, if more than one ...)": with three, the subsection still applies.
#ASSERT `Under section 61ZC(1), may I have both a Category A retirement pension because of units of additional pension and a Category B retirement pension, despite section 43` TRUE 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not covered: no Category B pension, so the subsection is not engaged and says nothing.
#ASSERT `Under section 61ZC(1), may I have both a Category A retirement pension because of units of additional pension and a Category B retirement pension, despite section 43` TRUE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: the Category A pension is not one because of s 61ZA, so s 61ZC(1) says nothing about it.
#ASSERT `Under section 61ZC(1), may I have both a Category A retirement pension because of units of additional pension and a Category B retirement pension, despite section 43` FALSE 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (I have a Category A pension, number of Category B pensions I have because of s 61ZB)
-- s 61ZC(2): a Category A pension together with one Category B pension because of s 61ZB; section 43 does not prevent both, so yes, they may.
#ASSERT `Under section 61ZC(2), may I have both a Category A retirement pension and a Category B retirement pension because of my late spouse's or civil partner's units of additional pension, despite section 43` TRUE 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not covered: no Category B pension because of s 61ZB.
#ASSERT `Under section 61ZC(2), may I have both a Category A retirement pension and a Category B retirement pension because of my late spouse's or civil partner's units of additional pension, despite section 43` TRUE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered: no Category A pension.
#ASSERT `Under section 61ZC(2), may I have both a Category A retirement pension and a Category B retirement pension because of my late spouse's or civil partner's units of additional pension, despite section 43` FALSE 2 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (paid in error because not an employed earner, the prescribed conditions are satisfied, the Inland Revenue think it appropriate, regulations so provide)
-- s 61A(2): the section applies, the Inland Revenue think it appropriate, and regulations provide for it.
#ASSERT `Under section 61A, are the contributions I paid in error treated as properly paid for my additional pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 61A(1): the contributions were not paid in error because the person was not an employed earner.
#ASSERT `Under section 61A, are the contributions I paid in error treated as properly paid for my additional pension` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 61A(1): the prescribed conditions are not satisfied.
#ASSERT `Under section 61A, are the contributions I paid in error treated as properly paid for my additional pension` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 61A(2)(b): the Inland Revenue are not of the opinion that it is appropriate.
