-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part ssc5 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for the seat layer ssc5-seat.l4: each is a person stating plain facts, with the answer the text gives.
-- Every expected value was decided from the section named in the question and written before the run.  A
-- question's arguments are in the order of its inputs in ssc5-seat.l4.  1 December 2025 was a Monday.

§ `Cases -- the individual's seat, Parts VI to X`

-- I was awarded arrears of pay under a reinstatement order: the whole sum is a mentioned sum.
#ASSERT `Under section 112(2), is a sum I was paid an employment protection entitlement` `s 112(3)(a) a sum payable in respect of arrears of pay in pursuance of an order for reinstatement or re-engagement under the Employment Rights Act 1996` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Only a part of a protective-award sum, and the part is not one regulations prescribe: "means" closes the definition.
#ASSERT `Under section 112(2), is a sum I was paid an employment protection entitlement` `s 112(3)(c) a sum payable by way of remuneration in pursuance of a protective award under the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I am abroad for the period, the benefit is under Parts II to V, and no regulations say otherwise.
#ASSERT `Under section 113(1), am I disqualified from receiving a benefit for a period` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I am in prison for the period.
#ASSERT `Under section 113(1), am I disqualified from receiving a benefit for a period` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither abroad nor in custody: the subsection does not speak.
#ASSERT `Under section 113(1), am I disqualified from receiving a benefit for a period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Regulations otherwise provide: the answer lies outside the Act.
#ASSERT `Under section 113(1), am I disqualified from receiving a benefit for a period` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Abroad: an increase for my wife, husband or civil partner shall not be payable.
#ASSERT `Under section 113(1), is an increase of benefit payable for my wife, husband or civil partner for a period` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Neither abroad nor in custody: the subsection does not speak.
#ASSERT `Under section 113(1), is an increase of benefit payable for my wife, husband or civil partner for a period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- I am a civil servant, not a member of the forces: the Parts apply as if I had a private employer.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(1), do Parts I to V of the Act apply to me as if I were employed by a private person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I serve in the forces in that capacity: subsection (1) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(1), do Parts I to V of the Act apply to me as if I were employed by a private person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not employed by or under the Crown: the subsection does not speak.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(1), do Parts I to V of the Act apply to me as if I were employed by a private person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- I am a member of the forces: my employment is not employed earner's employment for Part V.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(3), is my employment employed earner's employment for the purposes of Part V` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Neither: the subsection does not speak.
#ASSERT `Under section 115(3), is my employment employed earner's employment for the purposes of Part V` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- I serve in the forces: I am treated as an employed earner for Parts I to IV.
#ASSERT `Under section 116(1), am I treated as an employed earner because I serve in Her Majesty's forces` TRUE `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of Parts I to IV of this Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- For Part V, section 115(3) says my forces employment is not employed earner's employment.
#ASSERT `Under section 116(1), am I treated as an employed earner because I serve in Her Majesty's forces` TRUE `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of Part V of this Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I am not serving: the subsection speaks of a person while he is so serving.
#ASSERT `Under section 116(1), am I treated as an employed earner because I serve in Her Majesty's forces` FALSE `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of Parts I to IV of this Act` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Some other purpose: the subsection lists the purposes.
#ASSERT `Under section 116(1), am I treated as an employed earner because I serve in Her Majesty's forces` TRUE `s 116(1) some other purpose` EQUALS NOTHING
-- I worked on board a ship and regulations apply the provision to my accident.
#ASSERT `Under section 117, does my accident outside Great Britain fall within the exception for ships, hovercraft and aircraft` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No regulations apply: the exception exists only as regulations provide.
#ASSERT `Under section 117, does my accident outside Great Britain fall within the exception for ships, hovercraft and aircraft` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- I was outside Great Britain at a prescribed time and regulations apply the provision.
#ASSERT `Under section 119, does my accident outside Great Britain fall within the exception for persons outside Great Britain` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither: the exception exists only as regulations provide.
#ASSERT `Under section 119, does my accident outside Great Britain fall within the exception for persons outside Great Britain` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- I work on an offshore rig: the activities fall within the Petroleum Act section.
#ASSERT `Under section 120(2), is my employment in connection with continental shelf operations` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The activities do not fall within the Petroleum Act section.
#ASSERT `Under section 120(2), is my employment in connection with continental shelf operations` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Continental shelf work, prescribed employment, regulations apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 120, does my accident outside Great Britain fall within the exception for continental shelf workers` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not prescribed employment: the exception exists only as regulations provide.
#ASSERT `Under section 120, does my accident outside Great Britain fall within the exception for continental shelf workers` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 5 April 2024 is the last day of the tax year that began on 6 April 2023.
#ASSERT `Under section 122(1), in which tax year does a date fall` (Date 5 4 2024) EQUALS 2023
-- 6 April 2024 begins a tax year.
#ASSERT `Under section 122(1), in which tax year does a date fall` (Date 6 4 2024) EQUALS 2024
-- The last day of 2024-25 (5 April 2025) is a separate, 53rd tax week.
#ASSERT `Under section 122(1), in which tax week of its tax year does a date fall` (Date 5 4 2025) EQUALS 53
-- 6 April 2025 begins tax week 1 of 2025-26.
#ASSERT `Under section 122(1), in which tax week of its tax year does a date fall` (Date 6 4 2025) EQUALS 1
-- Wednesday 3 December 2025: the week begins on Sunday 30 November 2025.
#ASSERT `Under section 122(1), on what day does the Sunday-to-Saturday week containing a date begin` (Date 3 12 2025) EQUALS Date 30 11 2025
-- A lower earnings limit of 100 pounds a week (an arbitrary figure, as the limit is an input): 100 times 52.
#ASSERT `Under section 122(1), what is the qualifying earnings factor for a tax year` 100 EQUALS 5200
