-- An order specifies 9 pounds, which is not larger than 10.
#ASSERT `Under section 148(3)(b), how much is my Christmas bonus in pounds` TRUE 9 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A sum has already been paid in respect of me: only one sum shall be payable.
#ASSERT `Under section 148(5), is a further Christmas bonus payable in respect of me` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No sum has been paid yet: the subsection does not say a first one is payable.
#ASSERT `Under section 148(5), is a further Christmas bonus payable in respect of me` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A retirement pension is a qualifying benefit.
#ASSERT `Under section 150(1), is a payment I receive a qualifying benefit for the Christmas bonus` `s 150(1)(a) a retirement pension` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A kind the subsection does not list: the list is a definition by "means".
#ASSERT `Under section 150(1), is a payment I receive a qualifying benefit for the Christmas bonus` `s 150(1) a payment of some other kind` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2025: 1 December is a Monday, the first Monday in December.
#ASSERT (`Under section 150(4), which is the relevant week for the Christmas bonus in a year` 2025 FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 1 2000))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 1 12 2025
-- 2026: 1 December is a Tuesday, so the first Monday is 7 December.
#ASSERT (`Under section 150(4), which is the relevant week for the Christmas bonus in a year` 2026 FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 1 2000))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 7 12 2026
-- An order specifies another week, which replaces the first week in December.
#ASSERT (`Under section 150(4), which is the relevant week for the Christmas bonus in a year` 2026 TRUE (Date 9 12 2026) (Date 15 12 2026))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 9 12 2026

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part ssc6 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for ssc6-seat.l4: the questions of a person who works or claims statutory pay (ss 151-171ZT).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the Act's text (ukpga-1992-4.txt, lines 3095-3717), beside
-- the case. None is copied from what the code printed. A case marked "not covered" asserts NOTHING: the
-- text leaves the case to regulations or is silent on it, which is not a "no".
-- Arbitrary dates: 4 January 2026 is a Sunday; 8 November 2026 is a Sunday.
-- Figures regulations would supply (the lower earnings limit, a prescribed weekly rate) are arbitrary here.


§ `Part XI -- Statutory Sick Pay (ss 151-163)`

-- A Wednesday 14 January 2026 in my period of entitlement that began Monday 12 January: unable to work, qualifying day agreed.
#ASSERT `Under section 151, is my employer liable to pay me statutory sick pay for a day` (Date 14 1 2026) TRUE FALSE (Date 12 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not unable to work, and no rule treats me as unable: the day is not a day of incapacity for work.
#ASSERT `Under section 151, is my employer liable to pay me statutory sick pay for a day` (Date 14 1 2026) FALSE FALSE (Date 12 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The day is after my period of entitlement ended on 13 January.
#ASSERT `Under section 151, is my employer liable to pay me statutory sick pay for a day` (Date 14 1 2026) TRUE FALSE (Date 12 1 2026) TRUE (Date 13 1 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A circumstance in Schedule 11 stops a period of entitlement arising.
#ASSERT `Under section 151, is my employer liable to pay me statutory sick pay for a day` (Date 14 1 2026) TRUE FALSE (Date 12 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- We agreed qualifying days and the day is not one of them.
#ASSERT `Under section 151, is my employer liable to pay me statutory sick pay for a day` (Date 14 1 2026) TRUE FALSE (Date 12 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No agreement, and regulations make the day a qualifying day.
#ASSERT `Under section 151, is my employer liable to pay me statutory sick pay for a day` (Date 14 1 2026) TRUE FALSE (Date 12 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A term that tries to exclude part of the sick pay rules.
#ASSERT `Under section 151, is a term in my agreement with my employer void` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A term that does neither: the text does not say it is valid, so it is not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 151, is a term in my agreement with my employer void` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Earlier period ended 1 January 2026, later began 27 February: 56 days between, not more than 8 weeks.
#ASSERT `Under section 152, are my two periods of sickness treated as a single period of incapacity for work` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 27 2 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Later period began 28 February: 57 days between, more than 8 weeks, so the text does not treat them as one (not covered).
#ASSERT `Under section 152, are my two periods of sickness treated as a single period of incapacity for work` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not pregnant; incapacity ended 20 January 2026; nothing else has ended it.
#ASSERT `Under section 153, on what day does my period of entitlement to statutory sick pay end` TRUE (Date 20 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 20 1 2026)
-- Incapacity ended 20 January but I reached the maximum entitlement on 15 January: the earlier day.
#ASSERT `Under section 153, on what day does my period of entitlement to statutory sick pay end` TRUE (Date 20 1 2026) TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2026)
-- Pregnant; my maternity pay period begins 1 March 2026; nothing else has ended it: the day before, 28 February.
#ASSERT `Under section 153, on what day does my period of entitlement to statutory sick pay end` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- Pregnant, but my pregnancy ended before that period began other than by a confinement: limb (d) does not apply, and nothing else has ended it (not covered).
#ASSERT `Under section 153, on what day does my period of entitlement to statutory sick pay end` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- We agreed qualifying days and this is one.
#ASSERT `Under section 154, is a day a qualifying day for me` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- We agreed qualifying days and this is not one.
#ASSERT `Under section 154, is a day a qualifying day for me` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No agreement and regulations do not make it one.
#ASSERT `Under section 154, is a day a qualifying day for me` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Normal weekly earnings 100: weekly rate is 80 per cent, 80; 28 times 80 is 2240.
#ASSERT `Under section 155, what is the most statutory sick pay my employer must pay me in one period of entitlement` 100 EQUALS 2240
-- Normal weekly earnings 200: weekly rate is the 123.25 cap; 28 times 123.25 is 3451.
#ASSERT `Under section 155, what is the most statutory sick pay my employer must pay me in one period of entitlement` 200 EQUALS 3451
-- Liable apart from this rule, and not duly told.
#ASSERT `Under section 156, may my employer withhold my statutory sick pay for a day because they were not told in time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Liable apart from this rule, and duly told.
#ASSERT `Under section 156, may my employer withhold my statutory sick pay for a day because they were not told in time` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not liable apart from this rule: the rule speaks only of an employer who would be liable (not covered).
#ASSERT `Under section 156, may my employer withhold my statutory sick pay for a day because they were not told in time` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 80 per cent of 100 is 80, below the cap.
#ASSERT `Under section 157, what is my weekly rate of statutory sick pay` 100 EQUALS 80
-- 80 per cent of 200 is 160, above the cap of 123.25.
#ASSERT `Under section 157, what is my weekly rate of statutory sick pay` 200 EQUALS 123.25
-- Weekly rate 123.25 over 5 qualifying days is 24.65.
#ASSERT `Under section 157, how much statutory sick pay is payable for one qualifying day` 200 5 EQUALS JUST 24.65
-- Weekly rate 80 over 4 qualifying days is 20.
#ASSERT `Under section 157, how much statutory sick pay is payable for one qualifying day` 100 4 EQUALS JUST 20
-- A week with no qualifying day has nothing to divide by (not covered).
#ASSERT `Under section 157, how much statutory sick pay is payable for one qualifying day` 100 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Employed by the Crown, not serving in the forces.
#ASSERT `Under section 161, do the statutory sick pay rules apply to me as someone employed by the Crown` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Serving as a member of Her Majesty's forces, in that capacity.
#ASSERT `Under section 161, do the statutory sick pay rules apply to me as someone employed by the Crown` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not employed by the Crown: the section does not speak to this case (not covered).
#ASSERT `Under section 161, do the statutory sick pay rules apply to me as someone employed by the Crown` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Gainfully employed in Great Britain under a contract of service, with earnings.
#ASSERT `Under section 163, am I an employee for the purposes of statutory sick pay` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not gainfully employed.
#ASSERT `Under section 163, am I an employee for the purposes of statutory sick pay` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
