-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part ssc9 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for the seat layer ssc9-seat.l4. Every expected value is written by hand from the text, beside its assertion, and never copied from the encoding's output.
-- A result of NOTHING is the explicit "not covered" value: the text, read as the modules read it, does not answer. FALSE is the text's own no.

§ `Cases -- the seat questions for Schedules 5 to 13`


§§ `Schedule 5 -- deferred retirement pension`

-- A1: a deferment from 1 January to 31 December 2024 is 12 months complete: the duty to elect. A deferment one day short, or a person who is not deferred, is outside the paragraph's scope ('Where ... and the period of deferment is at least 12 months'), and the paragraph is silent about them: NOTHING, not a no.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph A1, must I choose between an increase of my pension and a lump sum` TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph A1, must I choose between an increase of my pension and a lump sum` TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 30 12 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph A1, must I choose between an increase of my pension and a lump sum` FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paragraph 1 (with 2): 6 incremental periods of 6 days (36 days of increment) at 1/5 per cent of 100 pounds is 6 x 0.20 = 1.20, which is at least 1 per cent of 100 (1.00): an increase of 1.20.
-- A deferment under 12 months needs no election. 12 days make 2 periods = 0.40, under the 1 per cent floor: no increase (0).
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 1, by how much a week is my retirement pension increased because I deferred it` TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 30 6 2024) `Under schedule 5 I made no choice within the prescribed period` 100 36 EQUALS JUST 1.2
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 1, by how much a week is my retirement pension increased because I deferred it` TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 30 6 2024) `Under schedule 5 I made no choice within the prescribed period` 100 12 EQUALS JUST 0
-- A deferment of 12 months or more: the increase applies only if the person elected it. No choice in time is treated as the lump sum (A1(2)), and the lump sum choice is the same: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 1, by how much a week is my retirement pension increased because I deferred it` TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2024) `Under schedule 5 I chose the increase of my pension` 100 36 EQUALS JUST 1.2
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 1, by how much a week is my retirement pension increased because I deferred it` TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2024) `Under schedule 5 I made no choice within the prescribed period` 100 36 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 1, by how much a week is my retirement pension increased because I deferred it` TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2024) `Under schedule 5 I chose the lump sum` 100 36 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paragraph 3A: a deferred person who chose the lump sum, or who made no choice (treated as the lump sum), is entitled to it; one who chose the increase, or is not deferred, is outside the paragraph.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 3A, am I entitled to a lump sum for deferring my retirement pension` TRUE `Under schedule 5 I chose the lump sum` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 3A, am I entitled to a lump sum for deferring my retirement pension` TRUE `Under schedule 5 I made no choice within the prescribed period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 3A, am I entitled to a lump sum for deferring my retirement pension` TRUE `Under schedule 5 I chose the increase of my pension` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 3A, am I entitled to a lump sum for deferring my retirement pension` FALSE `Under schedule 5 I chose the lump sum` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paragraph 3C: W entitled, W married to S when S died, S deferred when S died, S deferred throughout the 12 months ending the day before S died (1 Jan 2023 to 31 Dec 2023 is 12 months; starting 2 Jan 2023 is a day short).
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 3C, do I, as a widowed person, have a choice between an increase and a lump sum` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 1 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 3C, do I, as a widowed person, have a choice between an increase and a lump sum` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 2 1 2023) (Date 1 1 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 3C, do I, as a widowed person, have a choice between an increase and a lump sum` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 1 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paragraph 4: the increase to W is the increase S had, 4(1A); for a married person dying after 5 October 2002, or a civil partner on or after 5 December 2005, it is the basic increase plus half the additional (4(3)).
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 4, by how much a week is my pension increased because my late spouse or civil partner deferred theirs` (Date 6 10 2002) FALSE 10 6 EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 4, by how much a week is my pension increased because my late spouse or civil partner deferred theirs` (Date 5 10 2002) FALSE 10 6 EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 4, by how much a week is my pension increased because my late spouse or civil partner deferred theirs` (Date 5 12 2005) TRUE 10 6 EQUALS 13
-- Paragraph 7A: W to whom 3C applies is entitled to the lump sum when W elected it or made no choice in time (3C(3)); not when W elected the increase.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 7A, am I entitled to a lump sum because my late spouse or civil partner deferred their pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 1 2024) `Under schedule 5 I chose the lump sum` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 7A, am I entitled to a lump sum because my late spouse or civil partner deferred their pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 1 2024) `Under schedule 5 I made no choice within the prescribed period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 7A, am I entitled to a lump sum because my late spouse or civil partner deferred their pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 1 2024) `Under schedule 5 I chose the increase of my pension` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5 paragraph 7A, am I entitled to a lump sum because my late spouse or civil partner deferred their pension` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 1 2024) `Under schedule 5 I chose the lump sum` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Schedule 5A -- deferred shared additional pension`

#ASSERT `Under schedule 5A paragraph 2, by how much a week is my shared additional pension increased because I deferred it` TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 30 6 2024) `Under schedule 5 I made no choice within the prescribed period` 100 36 EQUALS JUST 1.2
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5A paragraph 2, by how much a week is my shared additional pension increased because I deferred it` TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 30 6 2024) `Under schedule 5 I made no choice within the prescribed period` 100 12 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5A paragraph 2, by how much a week is my shared additional pension increased because I deferred it` TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2024) `Under schedule 5 I chose the increase of my pension` 100 36 EQUALS JUST 1.2
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5A paragraph 2, by how much a week is my shared additional pension increased because I deferred it` TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2024) `Under schedule 5 I made no choice within the prescribed period` 100 36 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5A paragraph 4, am I entitled to a lump sum for deferring my shared additional pension` TRUE `Under schedule 5 I chose the lump sum` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5A paragraph 4, am I entitled to a lump sum for deferring my shared additional pension` TRUE `Under schedule 5 I made no choice within the prescribed period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 5A paragraph 4, am I entitled to a lump sum for deferring my shared additional pension` TRUE `Under schedule 5 I chose the increase of my pension` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Schedule 6 -- assessment of extent of disablement`

-- A prescribed loss of faculty is taken as 100 per cent whatever the assessor's figure; otherwise the assessor's figure.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 6 paragraph 1, what percentage disablement is assessed for me` TRUE 30 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `Under schedule 6 paragraph 1, what percentage disablement is assessed for me` FALSE 30 EQUALS JUST 30
-- Circumstances: age is allowed, any other particular circumstance is not; handedness is only for regulations under paragraph 2 to provide (NOTHING).
#ASSERT `Under schedule 6 paragraph 1, may my assessment take a particular circumstance of mine into account` `sch 6 para 1(c) the claimant's age` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 6 paragraph 1, may my assessment take a particular circumstance of mine into account` `sch 6 para 1(c) any other particular circumstance of the claimant` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 6 paragraph 1, may my assessment take a particular circumstance of mine into account` `sch 6 para 2 the claimant's being right-handed or left-handed` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The period starts no earlier than the day after the 90 days (Sundays disregarded) from the accident: an accident on Monday 4 November 2024 gives Sunday 16 February 2025.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 6 paragraph 6, from what day does the period taken into account by my assessment begin` (Date 4 11 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS (Date 16 2 2025)
#ASSERT `Under schedule 6 paragraph 6, from what day does the period taken into account by my assessment begin` (Date 4 11 2024) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS (Date 1 3 2025)
-- Under 14 per cent is a final assessment (6(3)); 14 or more is not decided; a latest part of 14 or more disapplies (6(5)(a)); the aggregation limbs together disapply (6(4)).
#ASSERT `Under schedule 6 paragraph 6, is my assessment a final assessment` 10 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 6 paragraph 6, is my assessment a final assessment` 14 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under schedule 6 paragraph 6, is my assessment a final assessment` 10 TRUE 20 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 6 paragraph 6, is my assessment a final assessment` 10 FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Schedule 7 Part I -- unemployability supplement`

#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 1, does the unemployability supplement Part apply to me` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 1, does the unemployability supplement Part apply to me` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Paragraph 2: incapable of work and permanently so: the pension is increased. Not incapable but earnings likely to be kept under the prescribed amount (104 or more): treated as incapable. Neither: not increased.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 2, is my disablement pension increased because I am incapable of work` TRUE TRUE FALSE 104 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 2, is my disablement pension increased because I am incapable of work` FALSE TRUE TRUE 104 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 2, is my disablement pension increased because I am incapable of work` FALSE TRUE FALSE 104 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 2, by how much a week is my disablement pension increased by the unemployability supplement` TRUE TRUE FALSE 104 30 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 2, by how much a week is my disablement pension increased by the unemployability supplement` FALSE TRUE FALSE 104 30 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Paragraph 3: a man under 60 gets the Schedule 4 amount (12.50); additional pension 20, less 4 units, less a Schedule 5 increase of 3 = 13, less a section 46 reduction of 5 = 8 is the relevant amount; 12.50 less 8 = 4.50.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 3, by how much a week is my unemployability supplement increased for my age, after the deductions` Man TRUE TRUE 12.5 TRUE TRUE 20 4 3 5 FALSE EQUALS JUST 4.5
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 3, by how much a week is my unemployability supplement increased for my age, after the deductions` Man TRUE TRUE 12.5 FALSE TRUE 20 4 3 5 FALSE EQUALS JUST 12.5
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 3, by how much a week is my unemployability supplement increased for my age, after the deductions` Man TRUE TRUE 12.5 TRUE TRUE 20 4 3 5 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 3, by how much a week is my unemployability supplement increased for my age, after the deductions` Woman TRUE FALSE 12.5 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 3, by how much a week is my unemployability supplement increased for my age, after the deductions` Woman FALSE TRUE 12.5 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 12.5
-- Paragraph 4: earnings of 243 against 215 and 28: the first child (243 is at least 215) and one further child (28 over 215 is one complete 28): 2 of 3 children get no increase. 214 withholds none. An order must name a LARGER amount.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 4, for how many of my children does my partner's pay mean I get no increase` TRUE TRUE 243 3 0 0 EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 4, for how many of my children does my partner's pay mean I get no increase` TRUE TRUE 214 3 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 4, for how many of my children does my partner's pay mean I get no increase` TRUE TRUE 280 3 250 30 EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 4, for how many of my children does my partner's pay mean I get no increase` TRUE TRUE 243 3 215 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 4, is my disablement pension increased for my children and qualifying young persons` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 4, is my disablement pension increased for my children and qualifying young persons` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 4, is my disablement pension increased for my children and qualifying young persons` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paragraph 5: contributions of 8 alone fall short of 10; with the other spouse's 3 they reach 11.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 5, is the condition on contributions to the cost of providing for my child satisfied` 8 FALSE 3 10 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 5, is the condition on contributions to the cost of providing for my child satisfied` 8 TRUE 3 10 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Paragraph 6: residing with a spouse gives the increase; contributing 20 against the 20 requisite rate also does; 19.99 does not.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 6, is my disablement pension increased for an adult dependant` TRUE TRUE 0 20 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 6, is my disablement pension increased for an adult dependant` TRUE FALSE 20 20 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 6, is my disablement pension increased for an adult dependant` TRUE FALSE 19.99 20 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 6, is my disablement pension increased for an adult dependant` FALSE TRUE 0 20 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paragraph 8: while the increase stands on the continued award, it is payable unless the relevant earnings exceed the amount (equal is payable).
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 8, is my increase still payable for a week when my partner's earnings have gone up` TRUE TRUE TRUE 30 40 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 8, is my increase still payable for a week when my partner's earnings have gone up` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 40 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 8, is my increase still payable for a week when my partner's earnings have gone up` TRUE TRUE TRUE 41 40 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 8, is my increase still payable for a week when my partner's earnings have gone up` FALSE TRUE TRUE 30 40 EQUALS NOTHING

