-- The rate is the lesser of 25 per cent of the last rate (40 gives 10) and 10 per cent of the maximum (200 gives 20): 10. The 9 April 1989 assumption is 26.96 (a quarter is 6.74). Half a penny and over is rounded up (10.005 gives 10.01); a fraction under half a penny is not dealt with (10.0025: NOTHING).
#ASSERT `Under schedule 7 paragraph 13, what weekly rate of retirement allowance do I get` FALSE FALSE 40 200 EQUALS JUST 10
