§§ `Schedule 10 -- priority between persons entitled to child benefit`

-- Paragraph 1: the person already awarded the benefit is the one entitled (up to the third week after the claim); the claimant is not. The fourth week after the claim confers no priority, and the later paragraphs decide.
#ASSERT `Under schedule 10 paragraphs 1 to 5, as between me and the other person, am I the one entitled to child benefit for the child` `Under schedule 10 I have already been awarded child benefit for that week when the other person claimed` 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Man FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `Under schedule 10 we have not jointly elected` FALSE `Under schedule 10 the Secretary of State has not decided` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 10 paragraphs 1 to 5, as between me and the other person, am I the one entitled to child benefit for the child` `Under schedule 10 I am the one claiming and the other person has already been awarded it` 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Man FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `Under schedule 10 we have not jointly elected` FALSE `Under schedule 10 the Secretary of State has not decided` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 10 paragraphs 1 to 5, as between me and the other person, am I the one entitled to child benefit for the child` `Under schedule 10 I have already been awarded child benefit for that week when the other person claimed` 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Man FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `Under schedule 10 we have jointly elected me` TRUE `Under schedule 10 the Secretary of State has not decided` EQUALS JUST TRUE
